{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.LogSineSharpConstant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.LogSineSharpConstant","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.EulerMaclaurinFirst","lean:module:QOU.Knot.LogSineSmoothPart"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phi_smooth_defect_sharp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phi_smooth_defect_sharp","kind":"theorem","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSharpConstant.lean#L278-L304","doc":"**L4-1 sharp constant (step 3, final form).**  The interior-cell smooth\ndefect equals the first Euler–Maclaurin term to within `O(h²)`:\n\n    | Σ_{i=1}^{n−1} ∫_{cell_i} (φ(x_{i+1}) − φ(u)) du\n          −  (h/2)·(φ(nh) − φ(h)) |   ≤   (h²/2)·(φ′(h) − φ′(nh)).\n\nThis is the `½` that `LogSineSmoothPart.smooth_defect_squeeze` provably\ncannot pin (measured: `computations/logsine_smooth_defect_constant.py`,\nwhere the scaled defect converges to the *midpoint* of the squeeze\ninterval, whose width does not shrink).  Effective and hypothesis-light:\nvalid for every `0 < h` and every `n ≥ 1` with `nh < π`; no limit is\ntaken, and no modulus of continuity is carried. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_phiDeriv_telescope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_phiDeriv_telescope","kind":"theorem","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSharpConstant.lean#L266-L276","doc":"**The two Riemann sums differ by exactly the endpoint gap** — the\ntelescope that makes the Euler–Maclaurin error `O(h²)` rather than `O(h)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phi_riemann_sum_bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phi_riemann_sum_bracket","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSharpConstant.lean#L228-L264","doc":"**`φ(nh) − φ(h)` is trapped between the same two Riemann sums** that\nbracket the cell-defect sum.  This is what converts the Euler–Maclaurin\nenvelopes into the identified term `(h/2)(φ(nh) − φ(h))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phi_sub_cell_bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phi_sub_cell_bracket","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSharpConstant.lean#L215-L226","doc":"**MVT bracket for `φ` on one cell** `[a, a+h] ⊆ (0, π)`: the increment is\ntrapped between `h·φ′` at the two endpoints, `φ′` being antitone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_Ico_one_telescope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.sum_Ico_one_telescope","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSharpConstant.lean#L203-L213","doc":"Telescoping a difference over `Finset.Ico 1 n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phi_interior_bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phi_interior_bracket","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSharpConstant.lean#L128-L178","doc":"**Step 3 — the Euler–Maclaurin bracket for `φ` on the interior cells.**\nOn the grid `x_i = i·h` with `nh < π`, the interior-cell defect sum\n(`i = 1 … n−1`, i.e. the cells covering `[h, nh]`) is bracketed by `h²/2`\ntimes the two endpoint Riemann sums of `φ′`:\n\n    (h²/2)·Σ φ′(x_{i+1})  ≤  Σ ∫_{cell_i} (φ(x_{i+1}) − φ(u)) du\n                          ≤  (h²/2)·Σ φ′(x_i).\n\nBoth envelopes are `(h/2)` times a Riemann sum of `φ′` over `[h, nh]`, so\nboth carry the first Euler–Maclaurin term `(h/2)(φ(nh) − φ(h))` — the `½`\nthe antitone squeeze could not pin.  The excluded `i = 0` cell needs no\nderivative: `smooth_defect_squeeze` already brackets it between\n`h·(φ(h) − log 2)` and `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phiDeriv_antitoneOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phiDeriv_antitoneOn","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSharpConstant.lean#L102-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.continuousOn_phiDeriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.continuousOn_phiDeriv","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSharpConstant.lean#L84-L100","doc":"**`φ′` is antitone** on any closed subinterval of `(0, π)` — the\nhypothesis the Euler–Maclaurin bracket needs.  `φ″ = 1/x² − 1/sin²x < 0`\nbecause `sin x < x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.hasDerivAt_phiDeriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.hasDerivAt_phiDeriv","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSharpConstant.lean#L66-L82","doc":"`φ″(x) = 1/x² − 1/sin²x` on `(0, π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.hasDerivAt_phi'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.hasDerivAt_phi'","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSharpConstant.lean#L63-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phiDeriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.phiDeriv","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSharpConstant.lean#L59-L61","doc":"`φ′` as an explicit function, matching `hasDerivAt_phi`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}